00:00:06.619 --> 00:00:09.770 align:start position:0%
for as long as I can remember I've  looked the same short and brown with  really big poofy hair I was pretty much  the same as any other kid in my school  except all the other girls had long  smooth straight hair when I watch TV  everyone else also had a long straight  hair that seemed to flow down their  backs like waterfalls the kids at school  would laugh and call me names like  poodle head or a big hair it got me  thinking maybe I should look like them  too so one day I decided to change I got  up one morning for school and flat  ironed my wild curls until they were  tame and manageable I actually felt  pretty happy with the result  I went to school that day feeling  amazing but of course it rained and by  the end of the day I had the same little  hair again I could hear all the kids at  school snickering that night I sat at  the dinner table and said mom I want a  perm we went to the salon the next  morning they washed my hair and covered  it with this thick smelly cream then I  sat there for what felt like hours I  could feel it stinging and burning at my  scalp but I told myself just ignore the  pain it'll all be worth it they finished  and just like that my hair was smooth  and flat perfect it was exactly what I  wanted but it didn't feel like it was  mine my wants long and bouncy curls now  fell against my face like thin lifeless  strings I gave myself some time to get  used to it but in that time some of my  hair began to shrivel and fall away I've  never been so mad at myself I gave up  something that made me unique just so I  could look like everybody else  eventually my hair grew back and so did  my courage I realized that no matter how  my hair looked it would never define who  I was  it was just hair and when I was all gone  I was still me I've still got poufy hair  but I embrace it every day because it's  mine
 

